Changelog: 17-10-2026 12:45:18

Release 0.2.0.

Changelog: 17-10-2026 12:29:59

Fixed. The app's folder in the suite is apps/vram (was apps/memory-manager) and its package is vram_manager (was
bc250_memory_manager): the suite's naming convention (owner, 17-10-2026), a short folder name and the package named
after what the app manages, without the BC-250 prefix; both names are the owner's. With the folder go its key in
the portal, its chapter of the wiki (apps/vram/, which the Manual link opens), its installer test and its release
tags: vram-v<x.y.z> from the next release on, which the app's update check follows. The installed app keeps its
name, its launcher bc250-memory-manager, its folder under ~/.local/share, its settings and the CMOS backups; the
CMOS helper still runs through pkexec from the app's folder. The portal moves its record of the installed copy to
the new key.

